  "descriptions": {
    "headline": "Where the sea is always moving.",
    "summary": "An elegant aquatic perfume reflects the depth of the sea & its fresh breeze in an oriental way.",
    "story": "Mawj is not a scent of sweetness or softness, but of power in motion. A wave that cannot be held back. A presence that arrives, lingers, and commands. Sea, water and ozone open it; bitter orange and pineapple cut across the top. Underneath, violet, iris and jasmine hold a quiet floral centre, and it dries down through vetiver, oud, musk and sandalwood into something warm and oriental — the depth of the sea rather than its surface.",
    "pullquote": "Not all waves are meant to be chased. Some are meant to be worn.",
    "persona": "Composed, deliberate, unhurried. Arrives before he speaks and is remembered after he leaves.",
    "best_for": [
      "Daytime and office wear",
      "Egyptian summer and coastal heat",
      "Long days that need to hold"
    ],
    "voice_register": "Declarative, elemental, masculine. Short lines with hard stops. Sea as metaphor for presence."
  },

